# The documented mixed-version residue is real: the model excludes a cross-shard
# straddler spanning a purge that finished on 10.2.0, and without that exclusion
# the property fails. The 10.2.0 purge raises no floor, L's catch-up raises only
# its own initiator's, and L's first initialisation claims only its own
# generation, so s2's straddler meets its still-loaded entry and is allocated
# above L's recorded close unless s2 re-seeds first. Operators should not purge
# trees during a rolling upgrade from 10.2.0.
MODULE: StraddlerBelowInitLegacyPurgeCrossShard
TARGET: StraddlerBelowInit
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a cross-shard straddler spans a purge that finished on 10.2.0
PERTURBS: LegacyPurge

--- FIND
    /\ ~recreated
    /\ ~pend["s2"]
--- REPLACE
    /\ ~recreated
\* MUTATION: a cross-shard straddler may span the 10.2.0 purge.
--- END
